@page "/components/command"

<PageTitle>Command — Unpoly.Blazor.Shadcn</PageTitle>

<h1 class="doc-h1">Command</h1>
<p class="doc-lede">
    A command palette without cmdk. Every item is already in the DOM as a real link and the
    compiler hides the ones that do not match — so it is a filtered list with JavaScript and a
    plain list of links without it.
</p>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Basic</h2>
<Example Source="CommandExample.razor"><CommandExample /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Command Palette</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    <code>Key="mod+k"</code> binds the shortcut — <code>mod</code> is ⌘ on a Mac and Ctrl
    everywhere else, which is the part implementations get wrong in one direction or the other.
    The search box in this site's own header is this component.
</p>
<Example Source="CommandDialogExample.razor"><CommandDialogExample /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Shortcuts</h2>
<Example Source="CommandShortcuts.razor"><CommandShortcuts /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Groups</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    A group whose every item is filtered out hides itself, heading and all: a heading over nothing
    is worse than no heading.
</p>
<Example Source="CommandGroups.razor"><CommandGroups /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Scrollable</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    The highlighted row is kept in view with <code>block: "nearest"</code> — nearest rather than
    centre, or arrowing down one row jumps the whole list.
</p>
<Example Source="CommandScrollable.razor"><CommandScrollable /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">When the list is too long to render</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    Filtering in the browser is right for a list the server already sent. For a catalogue of ten
    thousand, put <code>up-autosubmit</code> and <code>up-target</code> on the input and let the
    server answer — <code>&lt;CommandList&gt;</code> is the fragment it swaps, and the markup is
    otherwise identical.
</p>

